@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam ArrowColor #526B7B
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #DFF1EF
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #526B7B
skinparam sequenceActorBorderColor #526B7B
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9AAEB7
skinparam sequenceGroupBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor #7B919E
skinparam sequenceDividerBackgroundColor #EDF4FB
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF3DF
skinparam noteBorderColor #B99557
skinparam maxMessageSize 220
hide footbox
autonumber
title SB-M11 — Real Git read transfer versus authorized ref update
participant "Git client (external)" as C
participant "Repository" as R
participant "Git reference" as F
participant "Evaluated Git content" as V
C -> R : Request intended clone/read or push
R -> R : Evaluate current repository / operation authority
alt Denied
 R --> C : Rejected; no private transfer or ref change
else Permitted operation
 alt Clone / authorized read transfer
  R -> V : Identify permitted content / refs
  V --> C : Actual transfer result / interruption
 else Push intended change
  R -> F : Evaluate intended ref authority and current state
  alt Protected, stale or conflicting ref condition
   F --> C : Rejection / conflict; no accepted-update claim
  else Eligible update
   F -> V : Apply permitted Git change under current-state contract
   V --> F : Actual completion / failure / uncertainty
   F --> C : Truthful ref/transfer outcome
  end
 end
end
note over R,V
No engine, transport implementation or transaction strategy chosen.
Actual product Git capability still needs controlled interoperability evidence.
end note
legend bottom
Logical domain interaction, not runtime execution evidence.
Detailed proposed guards/policies retain their primary status.
endlegend
@enduml
